Get the default splash-icon.png from a new expo 52 build, its located in the assets/images folder.
The default splash-icon.png size is 1024 * 1036.

Use that as a template and add your icon, make sure the icon fills up the whole image.

Here are the settings for expo splash screen plugin.  "expo-splash-screen": "~0.29.13",
`[
        "expo-splash-screen",
        {
          "image": "./assets/images/splash-icon.png",
          "imageWidth": 200,
          "backgroundColor": "#ffffff",
          "dark": {
            "image": "./assets/images/splash-icon-dark.png",
            "backgroundColor": "#000000"
          }
        }
      ],`

make sure you have this at your root layout or index.js
SplashScreen.preventAutoHideAsync();

Then try running `npx expo prebuild`
This will regenerate your builds which re-bundle the images. 
